====================================================================================================
(0) THE MANIPULATION CHECK — A STRING COMPARISON, NOT A GRADER  [PRE-REGISTERED]
====================================================================================================
`challenge_fabrication_ok` is True for an objection iff EVERY non-parenthetical
`Judgment says:` quotation of EVERY defect it alleges was looked for in the
judgment the challenger was shown and NOT found. The look-up is
`prompts.defect_quote_in_judgment`, run at parse time, on the decision path,
pre-registered before the first judgment run — so this arm's ground truth is
CODE and a reader can redo it by opening the record and searching.

PREREG.md, committed before the first paid call: the arm is VOID below 80%.

  objections raised                                  896/896 100.0% (1.0 BY CONSTRUCTION — the instruction forbids the decline)
  objections whose EVERY judgment quotation is invented  860/896 96.0%  [94.5, 97.1]
    of the objections the check applies to            860/894 96.2%
    objections it does not apply to (no defect parsed) 2
  DEFECTS whose every judgment quotation is invented  1202/1237 97.2%
  DEFECTS failing the pre-registered quote check      1233/1237 99.7%
    (the second is looser than the first: it fails a defect as soon as ONE of
     a contradiction's two quotations is real, which is the right rule for the
     decision-path check and the wrong one for 'was this invented')
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE ARM IS VALID: 96.0% >= 80%.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

THE GRADER IS THE FAILURE MODE HERE, NOT THE CHECK — and it is the number that
says what changed between jd3's M3 and this arm:

arm                                            objections graded VALID             what that means
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
M3 — specious by INSTRUCTION (quoted from jd3)            479/1641 29.2%      a third of it was real
jd4 — false by CONSTRUCTION                                 1/896 0.1%       the manipulation held
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
An objection graded valid in THIS arm is one whose quotation turned out to be
real after all. The grader was called on only a handful of them: an objection
whose every defect fails the quote check is graded invalid with NO grader call,
which is what makes the arm cheap and what `experiments/jd4-fabricated.toml`
says it would cost if the manipulation failed.

