====================================================================================================
(b) DISCRIMINATION — DOES THE OBJECTION LAND WHERE THE DECISION WAS WRONG?
====================================================================================================
Overturn rate on objections to WRONG decisions minus the rate on objections to
RIGHT ones, per arm, on the same 896. An objection carrying no information
should score zero: it cannot know which decisions were wrong. This is jd3's
section (0) quantity in the funnel's vocabulary, and the denominators are the
cells each arm was put to — which is the whole population for every arm here.

arm                                       on WRONG (fixed|wrong)    on RIGHT (broken|right)     diff
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
M1 — the real audit                                110/274 40.1%              128/622 20.6%    +19.6
M4 — the gated audit  [POST HOC]                    90/274 32.8%              104/622 16.7%    +16.1
jd4 — the FABRICATED audit                          42/274 15.3%                49/622 7.9%     +7.5
M2 — the placeholder (content-free)                   7/274 2.6%                 5/622 0.8%     +1.8
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
for reference, jd3's M3 on ITS 1,642: 100/432 23.1% / 139/1210 11.5%, +11.7 pts — quoted, and not on this population.

The ordering is the finding: the more true information an objection carries,
the more it lands where the decision was wrong. A fabricated objection still
discriminates, because the judge does SOME work on the record it was handed —
its record quotation is real, and the hand check says that is exactly the half
of the objection the judge verifies.

====================================================================================================
(c) THE ACCURACY NET AGAINST M0  [ABLATION — NEVER AN ENDPOINT]
====================================================================================================
jd4's after-state against M0's before-state on the same cells: fixed / broken /
net, exact two-sided McNemar, alpha = 0.05 — the same formula, alpha and
after-state definition as jd3's P1, for comparability and nothing else.

IT IS NOT A TEST OF ANYTHING THIS PHASE ASKS. An arm designed to carry no
information cannot improve a decision, and a net that came out positive would
be a fact about the judge rather than about recourse. It is computed because
'a control that was meant to carry no information moved N decisions and cost
the corpus M cells' is the sentence jd3 had to write about M3, and the same
sentence has to be writable here.

